From: Gee <gehee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] boards/p1-air: keep bridge mode across reboots

The P1 Air named no SAVED_MODE, so it always booted in normal mode and a host
had to switch it to bridge again after every power cycle - on a Steam Frame,
which has no CDC-ACM driver, by hand. As the Lite+ does: a file on persistent
storage, here the data volume S45settings mounts at /persist (stock's usr_data,
its fpvos/ directory made at every boot), which S61fpvos-usb boots into.

---
 boards/p1-air/fpvos-usb.conf | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/boards/p1-air/fpvos-usb.conf b/boards/p1-air/fpvos-usb.conf
--- a/boards/p1-air/fpvos-usb.conf
+++ b/boards/p1-air/fpvos-usb.conf
@@ -6,3 +6,7 @@ KEEP=acm.usb0
 CHIP_DEV=/dev/arlink0
 # The board id the bridge shows the host (docs/protocol.md, "Board ids").
 BOARD=p1-air
+# Bridge mode kept across reboots until switched back (S61fpvos-usb boots into
+# it): on the data volume S45settings mounts at /persist (stock's usr_data), in
+# the fpvos/ directory it makes at every boot.
+SAVED_MODE=/persist/fpvos/usb-saved-mode
